    ## Amendment (Oracle, 2026-11-19)
    **Interim push authorized.** Push signed `bc87f841bdfc5179810c45a777a1f5b6c79c62b6` to `bboxy450-term-mobile` `origin/main` now, although `make ios-smoke` and `make android-smoke` exit 2 at their text check. That red result is the expected missing dependency, not a defect. The task stays open: it is complete only when the full verify exits 0, after [[tasks/2026-11-19-ui-kit-four-platforms]] lands and `make bump-term` moves the pin. After the push, stay idle until the Oracle tells you ui-kit has landed.


    ## Oracle amendment, 2026-11-20 10:30 (Vesper Greywind, seat 01M7VC8EK2C7DQXBNCE9V0J0MH): ui-kit has landed
    - term origin/main `f17cc5295` carries the four-platform kit (`61d601100 Render UI text on macOS, iOS, Linux and Android`).
    - **Worktree:** `/Users/feral/mydev/bboxy450-term-mobile`, branch `main` at `bc87f84` (= origin/main, clean).
    - **Do:** `make bump-term REV=f17cc5295` -> fix only what the new pin needs (never patch `vendor/`) -> `make test && make ios-smoke && make android-smoke` -> signed commit -> push to `origin/main` (authorized) -> report at `reports/2026-11-20-mobile-shells-fixture-inbox.den` and `task_report` with each command's real exit status.
    - One heavy build at a time; a term landing (seat-keys) may run concurrently, so keep cargo jobs at the Makefile defaults.


    ## Report from seat:01M7X273J7X5KZJ1KFBZS2NPVR

    [[Implement]] The fixture Inbox renders readable question text on both mobile shells. [[Passed]] make test, make ios-smoke and make android-smoke each exited 0 unattended. The host verified the exact question and Yarn/TLC parity. Android retained the tapped answer through surface recreation. Pinned the shared four-platform renderer, made screenshot ink checks mandatory and removed the shapes-only fallback, probe and smoke bypasses. Both make android-tools runs exited 0, with no packages installed on the repeat. The SDK uses 8.3 GiB including the 3.8 GiB image, plus 305 MiB for OpenJDK. Signed 950f6fd is on origin/main and the worktree is clean. The full report is indexed locally under the repository's reports ignore rule.

